 "dossier": "AURON · 1 OF 3 “Start with this one.” Click its picture to begin. The others wait on the board. ESC SKIP THE GUIDE CHAPTER SELECT CHAPTER IV Bahamut 0 OF 19 BEATEN X I II III VII VIII IX X XII XIV XVII XVIII XXVII X-2 IV V VI XI XIII XV XVI Something she used to call by name Under the temple, in the hangar where Vegnagun used to stand, an aeon is waiting and it is not itself. Nobody cheers when this one is over. ATB FINAL FANTASY X I Seymour Flux II Lady Yunalesca III Braska's Final Aeon VII Seymour and Anima VIII Evrae IX Yojimbo X Seymour Natus XII Seymour Omnis XIV Isaaru XVII Sin: the Fins and the Core XVIII Sin: the Face XXVII Mirror Aeons FINAL FANTASY X-2 IV Bahamut V Vegnagun VI Leblanc XI Fallen Aeons XIII Trema XV The Den of Woe XVI Ixion LOCATION Bevelle Underground — Limbo BOSS Bahamut PARTY Y YUNA R RIKKU P PAINE BEST Not cleared LEFT/RIGHT CHOOSE · UP/DOWN GAME · ENTER BEGI",
 "prepText": "AURON · 2 OF 3 “Your party is ready.” The tabs are for later. Start the battle. ESC SKIP THE GUIDE PARTY PREP IV · BAHAMUT — BEVELLE UNDERGROUND — LIMBO Y Yuna LV 23 R Rikku LV 24 P Paine LV 25 CHAPTER DRESSPHERES STATS ACCESSORIES ITEMS FFX-2 · IV Bahamut Something She Named Two years on, the aeon Yuna once called by name is standing in the dark with nobody home behind its eyes. She tries to talk it down anyway, because that is what she knows how to do. Limbo, a thousand years dark nobody is home you don't get another option OBJECTIVES Survive a Mega Flare Land a 5-hit Chain Attack Defeat Bahamut TIP Magic Break first, five stacks — it caps Mega Flare at a sixth of its damage and Impulse at a sixteenth, and it stacks with Shell. START BATTLE Y Yuna LV 23 · 10 DRESSPHERES WHITE MAGE R Rikku LV 24 · 10 DRESSPHERES DARK KNIGHT P Paine LV 25 · 9 DRESSPHERES WARRIOR",
